@startuml
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC5 Return Rental, confirm and refund (Contract 28), W11 draft
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc5_confirm_rental_return.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc5_confirm_rental_return.puml
' Participants: classes of the logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.5, 3.7, 4.1 to 4.3; PaymentMethod of AD-08.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #444444
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam SequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F4F8FD
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam SequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EAF1FB
skinparam SequenceReferenceBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B8A04A
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam LegendBorderColor #1F4E79
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 190

title NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram: UC5 Return Rental, confirm and refund (Contract 28)

box "UI layer (ui.api)" #F4F8FD
  participant ":RentalReturn\nController" as Ctl
end box
box "Application / domain layer" #F4F8FD
  participant ":RentalReturn\nHandler" as H
  participant ":Payment\nMethods" as PMs
  participant "pm:\nPaymentMethod" as PM
  participant "rr:\nRentalReturn" as RR
  participant "rental:\nRental" as R
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F4F8FD
  participant ":PaymentService" as Pay
  participant ":CashDrawer" as Dr
  participant ":Transaction\nRepository" as Repo
  participant ":Receipt\nPrinter" as Pr
end box

ref over Ctl, H
  Only in 7b (amount still due): makePayment(amount, tenderType) before this operation,
  as in the design sequence diagram of UC1 (Contract 4), through PaymentMethods (AD-08).
end ref

== confirmRentalReturn() - Contract 28 ==
[-> Ctl : POST /api/rental-returns/{id}/confirm
Ctl -> H : confirmRentalReturn()
H -> RR : refundTotal()
RR --> H : amount

alt amount = 0 (damaged item, late fee above the deposit, 7b paid)
  note over H, RR
    No Refund is created; go to the completion.
  end note
else amount > 0
  H -> RR : rentalPayment() <<new>>
  RR -> R : payment()
  R --> RR : original: Payment
  RR --> H : original (tender of the rental, BR-08)
  H -> PMs : get(original.tenderType)
  PMs --> H : pm
  H -> PM : refund(original, amount)
  note right of PM
    Polymorphism (AD-08): the handler never checks the tender.
    Cash: CashPaymentMethod. Card: CreditCardPaymentMethod.
    Check: CheckPaymentMethod answers NEEDS_APPROVAL (9c, FR-25).
  end note
  alt cash (9a)
    PM -> Dr : open(CASH_REFUND, employeeID)
    Dr --> PM : OPENED (logged, IR-14)
    PM --> H : RefundOutcome CASH_PAID
  else credit card (9b)
    PM -> Pay : refund(RefundRequest)
    note right of Pay
      RefundRequest = transaction ID of the refund,
      payment reference of the rental (DR-19), amount.
      Timeout 10 s in the adapter (AD-07).
    end note
    Pay --> PM : PaymentResult
    opt NOT_AVAILABLE (9b2b): outcome unknown
      PM -> Pay : refundStatus(transactionID)
      Pay --> PM : PaymentResult
    end
    PM --> H : RefundOutcome CARD_REFUNDED (with reference),\nNEEDS_APPROVAL (declined, 9b2a) or PENDING (status unknown)
  else check (9c)
    PM --> H : RefundOutcome NEEDS_APPROVAL
  end
  H -> RR : addRefund(outcome) <<new>>
  RR -> RR : create Refund (tender, amount, state, reference)
  note right of RR
    Creator: the rental return records its Refund.
    The reference of a card refund is encrypted when
    it is saved (AD-09, data_model.md 4.3).
  end note
end

alt amount = 0, CASH_PAID, CARD_REFUNDED or PENDING
  H -> RR : complete() <<new>>
  RR -> R : close()
  R -> R : item.status = Available (undamaged)\nor Under maintenance (damaged)
  RR -> RR : isComplete = true
  RR --> H : AccountingRecord
  note right of RR
    Creator: the rental return has the data of the
    record (deposit, late fee, tax, refund, tax to be corrected).
  end note
  H -> Repo : saveCompleted(rr, record)
  note right of Repo
    ONE database transaction (AD-05, AD-06): rental return, refund,
    item status, the AccountingQueue record and the entry of
    store_sync_list. The Accounting System gets it later (IR-06).
  end note
  opt card refund (CARD_REFUNDED or PENDING)
    H -> Repo : addRefundStatus(refundID, state, reference)
    note right of Repo
      PENDING: listed on S-02 (findPendingRefunds, FR-77);
      checkRefundStatus asks again later. Nothing is paid in cash.
    end note
  end
  H -> Pr : print(receipt)
  Pr --> H : READY, NO_PAPER or ERROR
  H --> Ctl : refund state, receipt number
  [<-- Ctl : 200 CASH_PAID, CARD_REFUNDED or PENDING;\nrental return receipt (S-06)
else NEEDS_APPROVAL (card declined, or check)
  note over H, RR
    No cash is paid and nothing is saved yet: the Refund stays unpaid (Contract 28).
  end note
  H --> Ctl : NEEDS_APPROVAL, reason
  [<-- Ctl : 200 NEEDS_APPROVAL, D-01 opens
  ref over Ctl, RR
    approveCashRefund(managerID, pin, reason): the same operation as in UC2 (Contract 9),
    see the design sequence diagram of UC2. ManagerApproval checks the store manager,
    CashPaymentMethod opens the drawer, then the completion above.
  end ref
end

legend bottom left
  **GRASP**
  Controller: RentalReturnController and RentalReturnHandler, as in the other UC5 diagrams.
  Polymorphism, Protected Variations: the refund goes through PaymentMethod (AD-08), so a new tender changes no handler (NFR-09).
  Creator: RentalReturn creates its Refund and its AccountingRecord, because it has their data.
  Information Expert: Rental closes itself and sets the status of its item; RentalReturn knows the refund amount and the tender of the rental.
  Low Coupling, Indirection: the handler sees only interfaces (PaymentService, CashDrawer, TransactionRepository, ReceiptPrinter);
  the timeouts are in the adapters and the fallbacks in the handler (AD-07).
endlegend
@enduml
